        "description": "Cape Canaveral, 2009-06-18. LRO (Lunar Reconnaissance Orbiter) — NASA's lunar surveyor for the modern era. Co-launched with LCROSS, which impacted into Cabeus crater 4 months later to confirm water ice in permanently-shadowed regions."
